      "id": 1,
      "code": "S",
      "title": "3 golden rules of English",
      "rule": "Ingliz tilida har bir gap 3 ta oltin qoidaga boʻysunadi. 1-qoida: har gapda EGA bor — kim yoki nima haqida gapiryapmiz (*I, you, he, she, it, we, they* yoki ism: *Dilnoza, the cat*). 2-qoida: har gapda FEʼL bor — ega nima qiladi yoki qanday (*am, is, are* yoki *go, like, work*). Oʻzbekchada \"Men oʻquvchiman\" da feʼl yoʻq, inglizchada esa *am* shart: *I am a student.* 3-qoida: soʻz tartibi doim bir xil — EGA + FEʼL + qolgani: *Dilnoza + lives + in Usmat.* Oʻzbekchadagi kabi feʼlni oxiriga qoʻymaymiz.",
      "examples": [
        "I am a student.",
        "Dilnoza is a teacher.",
        "We live in Usmat.",
        "Bekzod likes football.",
        "The cat is under the table.",
        "They go to school."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "subject", "uz": "ega" },
        { "en": "verb", "uz": "feʼl" },
        { "en": "sentence", "uz": "gap" },
        { "en": "word order", "uz": "soʻz tartibi" },
        { "en": "live", "uz": "yashamoq" },
        { "en": "like", "uz": "yoqtirmoq" },
        { "en": "go to school", "uz": "maktabga bormoq" },
        { "en": "every day", "uz": "har kuni" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Dilnoza and her family",
        "en": "Hello! I am Dilnoza. I am a teacher. I live in Usmat. Usmat is a small town. My brother is Bekzod. He is a student. He likes football. We have a cat. The cat is Tom. Tom is under the table. My mother is a nurse. My father is a farmer. We are a happy family."
      },
